# WinClash GAMEPLAY (Baccarat) bot: the casino/hedge commands
# (/testbaccarat, /pair, /pairs, /delpair, /run, /stoprun, /runs, /runlog)
# driving Evolution Baccarat on winclash.com -- acc1 always bets Banker,
# acc2 always bets Player on the SAME hand at the SAME table, so the money
# mostly moves between the two accounts and only the ~5% banker commission
# bleeds. Same flow as .env.gameplay (cricmatch) and .env.winclash.stockmarket,
# just pointed at winclash's Baccarat table. No signup commands -- those live
# on .env.winclash.
#
# WHAT IS VERIFIED LIVE ON THIS SITE (2026-08-29), so nobody re-derives it:
#   * login()          -- real account, real session, confirmed through the
#                         site's own POST /api/getBalance.
#   * the table route  -- winclash has no usable lobby tile (hover-only,
#                         paginated behind a JS-state search box, and its
#                         handler refuses to launch on a zero balance), so
#                         the engine navigates straight to the site's own
#                         /casinoRedirect launch URL. That lands on
#                         ezugi.evo-games.com -- the same Evolution client
#                         every other site here drives.
#   * the whole read path on an Evolution table reached that way
#                      -- verify_stockmarket.py PASSED end to end (table
#                         ready ~37s, balance / TOTAL BET / chip rail all
#                         readable, 4 clean betting windows in 90s).
#
# WHAT IS *NOT* VERIFIED, and it matters before any real run:
#   * NO BET HAS EVER BEEN PLACED ON WINCLASH, on any table. The only account
#     available during development held 0.00, so placing, settling and the
#     hedge itself are untested here -- everything above is a read.
#   * THE BACCARAT TABLE ITSELF HAS NEVER BEEN OPENED HERE. Only Stock Market
#     (id 1027) has. sites/winclash.py carries "Baccarat A" as id 86 from
#     winclash's own /casinoGamesList; re-confirm it before trusting it:
#         .venv/bin/python probe_winclash_games.py <user> <pass> --find baccarat
#     (read-only -- it opens no table and places no bet). A wrong id opens
#     the wrong table; the run then fails on the bet-spot check rather than
#     betting wrongly, but you would be debugging the wrong thing.
#   * THE TABLE MINIMUM IS UNKNOWN on winclash. cricmatch's Baccarat A is
#     100 rupees a side; do not assume winclash matches until /testbaccarat
#     reports a confirmed TOTAL BET.
#   * Which key of /api/getBalance carries the real figure (see
#     sites/winclash.py -- wallet vs main_balance/totalBalance both read 0.00
#     on an empty account, which cannot tell them apart).
#
# So, in order: fund two accounts, run
#     /testbaccarat <user> <pass> 100
# (that confirms login + the launch URL + a real Baccarat table + a real
# placement, and reports the actual TOTAL BET), then a single
#     /run <pair> <table minimum> 1
# and read /runlog before scaling either the amount or the rounds.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your-winclash-gameplay-bot-token-from-botfather
# One id, or several comma-/space-separated ids for multiple master admins:
# MASTER_ADMIN_ID=111111111,222222222
MASTER_ADMIN_ID=your-telegram-user-id

# REQUIRED on winclash, unlike cricmatch/khelofun. Every page load here can be
# met by an AWS WAF interstitial, and the WAF also gates the login CALL itself
# (405 + x-amzn-waf-action: captcha) after a stretch of logins from one IP.
# The soft "challenge" clears itself for free; the hard "captcha" needs a
# solved token, and each seat's login pays one if it lands on that. Without a
# key a run fails with a clear message rather than hanging.
CAPSOLVER_API_KEY=your-capsolver-api-key

BOT_MODE=gameplay
BOT_SITE_URL=https://winclash.com/
ADMINS_FILE=admins.winclash.gameplay.json
SETTINGS_FILE=bot_settings.winclash.gameplay.json
ADMIN_PHONES_FILE=admin_phones.winclash.gameplay.json
# Pair credentials + run history. MUST be distinct from every other
# instance's files -- each process reads them once at import and rewrites
# them whole on every save, so two bots sharing a path silently clobber
# each other. (pairs.* holds plaintext passwords; both patterns are
# gitignored.)
PAIRS_FILE=pairs.winclash.gameplay.json
PAIR_RUNS_FILE=pair_runs.winclash.gameplay.json

# How many /run hedge sessions may execute at once (each drives two Chromium
# browsers). Default 3. The WAF block above is per exit IP and behavioural,
# so more concurrency without more proxy IPs makes it worse, not faster.
# MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=3
